%% data-flow-sequence.mmd
%% Shows: a single snapshot request traced through every plane.
%% Companion to: docs/tutorial/01-planes-and-data-flow.md

sequenceDiagram
    actor Eng as QA Engineer
    participant UI as UI
    participant CP as Control Plane
    participant SGP as Security/Governance
    participant MP as Metadata Plane
    participant DP as Data Plane
    participant OS as Object Storage

    Eng->>UI: Request snapshot (dataset, sizing rule, cadence)
    UI->>CP: POST /snapshot-requests
    CP->>SGP: Authorize(user, action, classification tier)
    SGP-->>CP: allow / deny + audit event emitted
    CP->>MP: Resolve policy + classification for dataset
    MP-->>CP: policy version, classifications
    CP->>MP: Check footprint/quota for target environment
    MP-->>CP: within quota
    CP->>DP: Submit job DAG (subset -> mask -> certify)
    DP->>OS: Read source-shaped data (staging)
    DP->>DP: Subset (referential integrity preserved)
    DP->>DP: Mask (deterministic, keyed - ADR-0006)
    DP->>DP: Certify output against policy
    DP->>SGP: Record certification evidence
    DP->>MP: Write lineage (job run, inputs, policy version)
    DP->>OS: Publish snapshot (versioned)
    DP->>MP: Register snapshot (version, location, row counts)
    CP-->>UI: Job complete, snapshot ready
    UI-->>Eng: Snapshot available + certification status
